text:
Treasure hunt.
#bee #flowers #spring #pollen 
@ctccct @Whatsgrowingon1 @MinterGardening @butchartgardens http://t.co/xAWWo42S3j

@TechnicallyRon Lest you think I joke about April, let me tell you about the Fruitless Mulberry. Fine tree, big leaves, loads of shade.

Produces absurd amounts of pollen.

And no, I don't mean September is that hot. It's actually fairly pleasant. I mean that wildfires are a thing here.

@KathyOrrFOX29 @FOX29philly Hi Kathy,
Love warmer weather but I have one problem  pollen, everytime its humid I suffer
 with sinuses, my head feels like a truck ran me over, please tell Jim I know he feels

@TheFoofinator Be careful what you wish for cuz I'm about to spam you 😭😂:
Your glasses malfunction: what do you see?
The pollen fairies messed up and now some people have allergies in the spring: elaborate.

Get out early - Summer Sizzle later today!

 Itchy throat? High Pollen Count and Air Quality Alert Posted.  A/C will be our best friend later today for many reasons!

@KPRC2 @KPRC2WEATHER https://t.co/xToHUBrebN https://t.co/Sdlzso4DFL

WARM WEDNESDAY

Ready for 80 degrees? It could happen in a few spots today! Tomorrow could even be a couple degrees warmer. Now if we could just slow down the pollen...

@WSAVKrisA @wsavleeh @wsavalysac https://t.co/S9kakP0XLw

@JenKirkman Spring is UNEQUIVOCALLY the worst season. It is NO CONTEST!

Spring is bugs, and pollen, and rain, and mud. 

You like rebirth and blossoming? Read a poem.

@AmBoDe33 @JoeFultano 😂 

Pollen count has been very high some days here in RVA. I watch daily, for when I moved here I got so sick and someone at work said “It’s allergies” and I said “To what, trees? I don’t have allergies!”

Turns out a Claritin tablet fixed it and I take them every spring now. 😂 https://t.co/4YZva7oR13

Me - Ahh yeah! Beautiful spring weather!

*goes outside and sees neon yellow stippling on everything*

Me - Ahh no! Oak pollen season! ;A;

One of these pollens is making my face itch.... thank you spring. 

But important to note, the pollen count has nearly doubled since yesterday. The mold count also rose significantly. 
@wcpo #cincywx https://t.co/bynPBvY9uI

It won't be rainy all weekend, but you'll want to keep the umbrella handy. The silver lining is that pollen levels will be the lowest they've been all spring!!
#StormTracker8
@8NEWS https://t.co/xFBfNuYwsS

@crystalchappell That’s great, Crystal !!! I’m so excited for you and your entire cast and crew!  I’m here in Jersey, so welcome back to our area.
Hope the weather is decent and that your allergies are OK. Bring your allergy meds. The pollen count here has been outrageous!!!
Happy Mother’s Day!

@WayneDupreeShow Because we live among friends, loved ones and political foes in peace and liberty, let us always remember we have as many thoughts and opinions as are granules of pollen that paint a river bank after a long frigid spring.

We may respectfully disagree. 

We are free to do so.

@xchazzitupx 🍣 :3

Yeah, it's just terrible. :/ Yeah it happens. Asthma sucks. The winter effects mine honestly. Pollen and dust definitely mess with asthma during the spring.

Yes, it is always pretty around that time-

@TomJChicago #Itsoknottobescared of corona virus
We live in a soup of virus' and there is no master catalog
The government cannot protect you from pollen mold weather, pathogens, the S.A.D diet, etc nor would we want a government that powerful. Because who would protect us from them?

@luilui239 Interesting how these outbreaks always occur around spring/summer

Pollen's often seen as tree sperm but this makes it clear it's the mother's regeneration

References to the spine, murus/surum/serum, brochi/lungs🍀 which Covid affects https://t.co/csSGLX6BI8

@TheScalpeledge @textranquilo @RichHiggins_DC @charliekirk11 Do you think the end of flu season and hopefully the end of Corona season could have more to do with pollen than temperature?
Pollen must have a antiviral mechanism to prevent plants having their DNA corrupted.
Right now could we be breathing an antiviral?

@lstn2urmama @papawat1 @gatewaypundit As with most meds..
I’m on high dose of unpasteurized honey to help battle spring pollen related allergy’s..
I’m buzzing all day🤡🤦‍♂️

@MaybeAmes Went to visit my sister in Daytona...will stay in area for week.  Area is dead near the speedway

My sinuses are blowing up.  It has been hot in FL (90s) and pollen everywhere.  

Absolutely disappointed in that presser.  America cannot wait until Apr 30th.  That is insane

Wake up and smell the flowers some time... 👃

@StripperAtlanta

#flower #juicy #epic #nsfw #drip #ooze #creampie #spring #pollen #allergy #atl @ Atlanta, Georgia https://t.co/9RjQIMs9SJ

@ErickAdameOnTV @NY1weather TRANSLATION Dont freak out if you sneeze, its allergies from the pollen- not the Virus. Dont Sneeze on people. 
Rain on Monday should wash away the germs which were sneezed everywhere.
#CoronaVirusUpdate

@ericfisher are there weather apps other than accu weather, that give an accurate account of allergies? I always feel like I’m being gaslit with accu🤷🏽‍♀️
Them: Allergies, ALL: low -none
Me: eyes burning, pollen floating in the air, grass flying, car covered in green. . .

@MumT @toddeherman @JayInslee It's plenty hot in most of the US right now and it's not affecting it.
I suspect that the seasonality of virus has more to do with pollen than heat and sunlight.
Pollen has antivirals that could extend to us.

@DTrump_Cat Yes—the one with the pitted fruit allergy is also highly allergic to pollen. Spring is her most difficult season because it exacerbates her asthma.🥺
She’s in her late 20’s, lives alone and loves to exercise outdoors.
She takes multiple allergy meds, but I still worry.

@AutiLeven @bennessb Cool.
I know the weather app I have does like UV index and pollen. I'll have to look into some medical apps. Maybe there is one that is universal (based on gps).
And hopefully free lol

@seanmhoban Hi Sean, I hope you do well. I published a paper for pollen flow in black walnut with recording some phenology data. https://t.co/E8ecEeRHKD.
I am working on phenology of butternut but late spring frost-2020 did not let me to complete this study. 

Hopefully in 2021.

