Basically no hurricanes, no earthquakes, no tornadoes, less tree pollen. Warm summers, snowy winters, autumn colors.

Ticks suck, but our scientists are working on that.

@GretaThunberg @Peters_Glen Thanks for noting your shock, Greta!

In Virginia, being this warm has already impacted crop yield. Pollen of self-pollinating tomatoes becomes sterile above 85°F. Tomato plants in Northern VA only produced fraction of normal yield. 

One of my large plants only had 1 tomato😢

@stimmyskye No, you're not alone. I found that MCAS flares lend to this for me, and stress lends to both. #EDS 

